    "gitMarketplace.error.authRequired.tokenNoAccess.custom": "{host} reports no repository at this source's address to the token stored for {host}, so the token may lack access to it. Use Set token… on the source's row in Sources to replace it with one that can read the repository; if the address is wrong, use Remove source and add it again with the right one.",
